  "body": "What happens: the v0.19.0 release gate (tier release, tree 9047b5f6f on release/v0.19.0, same code as main 38699549e) fails in `camcraft-kernel`, test `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` (`crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs:357`): \"STEP verdicts changed, or a fixture has no row - re-triage\". This suite runs only in the release tier (kernel runs in release), so quick and batch gates did not show it.\n\nEvidence (gate-logs/release-20261113-113616/02-kernel_suites.log): the measured list holds rows the expected table lacks. Seen in the measured list and not in the expected one:\n- `bad_entity_mid_data.step`: import \"both refuse (solidcore: read_step: invalid input: STEP syntax error)\", mesh \"no exact solid to judge against\"\n- `lathe_holder_offset.step`: import \"agree\", mesh \"watertight, within tolerance\" (the assert output is cut off after `sample_ap214.step`, so check this one and the rest of the list)\nThe verdicts of the fixtures that already have rows look unchanged; the fixtures were added by other PRs since v0.18.0 (the lathe holder fixture likely by PR 1061) without a row in this table.\n\nExpected: every STEP fixture in the scanned directory has a triaged row, and the test passes in release.\n\nDone means: `cargo test --release -p camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement` passes on main, with each new row read and triaged (a refusal by name or an agreement), not copied blindly; no fixture or golden is changed. This blocks the v0.19.0 cut.\n",
